{
  "$schema": "../schema.json",
  "name": "io.github.chandradot99/voicedex",
  "title": "Voicedex",
  "category": "AI, LLMs & Agents",
  "description": "Search, compare and price 800+ speech-to-text, text-to-speech and voice models from 120+ providers",
  "repository": "https://github.com/chandradot99/voicedex",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "search_models",
      "description": "Search active speech models. Filters combine (AND). Paged: pass next_offset to get more.\n\n    language: BCP-47 code, e.g. \"hi\" or \"en-GB\". Only models that explicitly list it are returned, unless\n    include_unlisted_languages=true also adds models that claim \"many languages\" without listing them. capability: one feature term, e.g. \"speaker_diarization\",\n    \"voice_cloning\", \"word_timestamps\", \"ssml\"; for realtime (sts) models \"function_calling\", \"turn_detection\",\n    \"barge_in\", \"transcription\", \"video_input\". streaming=true: models usable live (realtime transcription,\n    low-latency TTS, voice agents); batch=true: models that accept files / pre-recorded jobs (batch=false excludes\n    them; models whose batch support isn't documented are left out of either filter). max_price_usd: upper bound on the normalized price (TTS per 1M\n    characters, STT/STS per hour); models without a comparable USD price are excluded when it is set.\n    sort: default \"price\" (cheapest first, announced shutdowns after the rest, unpriced last), or \"eol_date\"\n    (soonest end first) whenever shutting_down or eol_before is set. Shutdowns: shutting_down=true returns only\n    models with an announced end date; eol_before=\"YYYY-MM-DD\" only those ending before it (e.g. \"which models\n    shut down in the next 90 days?\"). collapse_snapshots (default true) shows one row per model family (the\n    moving alias, e.g. gpt-realtime) and lists its dated snapshots (gpt-realtime-2025-08-28) in \"snapshots\";\n    pass false to get every snapshot as its own row. realtime=true: models served over WebSocket or WebRTC\n    (stricter than streaming). recommended=true: models the provider's docs point new integrations to.\n    preview=true: alpha/beta/preview models only (false excludes them). sort=\"newest\": latest release first.\n    framework: only models whose provider has a first-party integration for that model type in the framework's\n    own docs (LiveKit Agents, Pipecat, Vapi, Retell); each result lists them in works_with.\n    ",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "stt",
                  "tts",
                  "sts"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Type"
          },
          "language": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Language"
          },
          "capability": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Capability"
          },
          "provider": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Provider"
          },
          "region": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "us",
                  "eu",
                  "asia",
                  "global"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Region"
          },
          "max_price_usd": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Max Price Usd"
          },
          "open_weights": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Open Weights"
          },
          "streaming": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Streaming"
          },
          "batch": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Batch"
          },
          "realtime": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Realtime"
          },
          "recommended": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Recommended"
          },
          "preview": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Preview"
          },
          "framework": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "livekit",
                  "pipecat",
                  "vapi",
                  "retell"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Framework"
          },
          "query": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Query"
          },
          "include_unlisted_languages": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Include Unlisted Languages",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "shutting_down": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Shutting Down"
          },
          "eol_before": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Eol Before"
          },
          "sort": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "price",
                  "name",
                  "eol_date",
                  "newest"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Sort"
          },
          "collapse_snapshots": {
            "default": true,
            "title": "Collapse Snapshots",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "limit": {
            "default": 20,
            "title": "Limit",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "offset": {
            "default": 0,
            "title": "Offset",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "title": "search_modelsArguments"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "get_model",
      "description": "One model's record: pricing with all variants (e.g. streaming vs pre-recorded) and source, languages,\n    capabilities with notes (e.g. \"pre-recorded only, English only\"), regions, interfaces, audio formats,\n    limits, lifecycle, shutdown date and replacement, open-weights licence, provenance. model: key or loose name.\n    detail=\"compact\" (default) groups regional language codes and trims source URLs; \"full\" returns everything.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "model": {
            "title": "Model",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "detail": {
            "default": "compact",
            "enum": [
              "compact",
              "full"
            ],
            "title": "Detail",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "model"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "title": "get_modelArguments"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "compare_models",
      "description": "Compare up to 6 models side by side. Each item can be an exact key \"provider/type/model_id\" (from\n    search_models) or a loose name like \"deepgram nova-3\" or \"Cartesia Sonic 3\". A loose name resolves to the\n    best match and says so in matched_as (with other_candidates): tell the user what was assumed. Unmatched\n    items come back with \"did you mean\" suggestions when something is close.\n\n    Each model includes price (with source and check date), streaming / batch, languages, regions, interfaces,\n    limits (max_text_chars, max_audio_seconds), audio formats, sample rates, feature caveats\n    (capability_notes, e.g. \"pre-recorded only\"), open-weights licence and shutdown date. \"differences\" lists, in\n    plain words, every field and feature where the models disagree.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "models": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": "Models",
            "type": "array"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "models"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "title": "compare_modelsArguments"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "estimate_cost",
      "description": "Cost in USD for a workload, computed here so no unit conversion is left to the model.\n\n    models: keys or loose names (up to 6). characters: text to synthesize (TTS). audio_minutes: audio to\n    transcribe (STT/STS), or for TTS the minutes of speech to produce (converted with tts_chars_per_minute,\n    default 900 chars ≈ 150 words/min). Passing an STT and a TTS model with audio_minutes gives a voice-agent\n    pipeline estimate: STT transcribes all audio_minutes, TTS speaks tts_share of them (e.g. 0.5 if the agent\n    talks half the time); \"total_usd\" sums the models (LLM and telephony not included). Uses each model's headline\n    pay-as-you-go price unless a separate streaming rate applies: mode=\"streaming\" (the default \"auto\" picks it\n    whenever an STT/STS model is costed together with a TTS model, i.e. a live voice agent) uses the\n    provider's published pay-as-you-go streaming rate where there is one; mode=\"batch\" uses the headline\n    (often pre-recorded) rate. Each line's rate_used says which. Volume discounts, free tiers and plan\n    prices are not applied.\n    ",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "models": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": "Models",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "characters": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Characters"
          },
          "audio_minutes": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Audio Minutes"
          },
          "tts_chars_per_minute": {
            "default": 900,
            "title": "Tts Chars Per Minute",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "tts_share": {
            "default": 1,
            "title": "Tts Share",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "mode": {
            "default": "auto",
            "enum": [
              "auto",
              "streaming",
              "batch"
            ],
            "title": "Mode",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "models"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "title": "estimate_costArguments"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "find_alternatives",
      "description": "Replacements for a model (e.g. one that is shutting down): active models of the same type, ranked by how\n    many of its explicitly listed languages they cover, then shared features, then how close the price is. The\n    provider's own announced successor, if any, comes first. model: key or loose name.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "model": {
            "title": "Model",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "limit": {
            "default": 10,
            "title": "Limit",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "model"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "title": "find_alternativesArguments"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "search_voices",
      "description": "Search stock voices (15,000+, so results are compact and paged: pass next_offset for more).\n    model: a model id of that provider (voices compatible with it). has_sample=true returns only voices with\n    an audio preview URL. use_case / age / accent (e.g. \"British\", \"Indian\") filter on values normalized from\n    each provider's free-text tags; a voice without that information never matches. emotion=true: voices with\n    emotion control; multilingual=true: voices that speak several languages. Results list voices with a sample\n    first, then widely used providers.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "provider": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Provider"
          },
          "language": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Language"
          },
          "gender": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "male",
                  "female",
                  "neutral"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Gender"
          },
          "model": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Model"
          },
          "has_sample": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Has Sample"
          },
          "use_case": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "enum": [
                  "Conversational",
